# systemd --user enable writes real symlinks into these dirs. Since ~/.config
# symlinks straight into this repo (stow tree-folding), those enable symlinks
# land in the working tree - but they're absolute paths baked to one user's
# $HOME, so they aren't portable to commit. Recipes call `systemctl --user
# enable` themselves so this state gets regenerated correctly per machine.
**/systemd/user/*.wants/
